{"text": "mL45@\n\nDie Neve Arztliches Thursday 19th Hay 1988\nPie Neue Arztliche, Thursday 19th Nay 1988\n\nClinics And Doctors\" Practices\nGlinics And Doctors\u2019 Practices\n\nStudies Reveal A Trend Towards Carcinogenit,\nStudies Reveel A Trend Towards Carcinogenity\nDISPUTE ABOUT PASSIVE SHOKING GOES ON\nDISPUTE ABOUT PASSIVE SHOKING GOES ON\n\nFor aany years scientists and lay people have been arguing vhether\nPassive seoking is injurious to health and. if so, to vhat degree. In the\ncourse of the debate sany people have even asserted that. in exactly the\nsame way as active inhalation, passive saoking may cause lung cancer.\n\nHowever @ full-dey's hearing in Vienna, to which the Austrian\nMinister Of Health, Dr. Franz LBschnak hed been invited and vhich vas\nattended by 22 scientists froa Austria, West Germany. the USA and Denaarky\nGesonstrated that no unequivocal settleaent of this dispute 1s currently\nin sight. Professor Karl Oberla of the \"Institute For Hedicinal Inforsacion\nProcessing, Statistics And Biosathesetics\u201d at the Grosshadern Clinic of\nMunich University reported.that all previous studies purporting to show\nthat passive saoking increases the risk of lung cancer exhibit considerable\nfaults in respect of the forsulation of questions and study design. He\nsaid that he was of the opinion that \u2018oa closer examination not a great deal\ncould be sade of all the evidence\". Neta-analyses which had atteapted to\ncollate several studies into one definitive statement. had generally failed\non account of unsatisfactory cosparability and inadequate quality.\n\nMerla asserted that careful examination of the studies indicated\nthat pessive seoking could not be shown to increase the risk of lung\nCancer and added in his omn words, \"Epidentology does not have the mission\nof improving the world. It aust not succum to the spirit of the tines\n\u2018end supply imprecise proofs. The question of whether passive saoking is\ninjurious to health 1s open. A certain effect cannot be excluded but it\nis likely to be slight\u201d.\n\ngevetstz0z",
